			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Replay SCM resource groups and persist snapshots for late subscribers\n\nCocoon fires `register_scm_resource_group` before SkyBridge's listener is attached (Tauri events are not buffered), so the workbench booted with the SCM provider header visible but zero groups — and even when `update_scm_group` arrived, the resource tree stayed empty because the event was consumed without persisting the snapshot for boot-time replay.\n\n- **UpdateScmGroup**: Persist each incoming `ResourceStates` array into MarkerState as `SourceControlManagementResourceDTO` entries keyed by `(ProviderHandle, GroupId)`, so the replay loop can re-emit the latest snapshot.\n- **ReplayEvents**: Add two new replay legs — group registration (`sky://scm/registerGroup`) and resource update (`sky://scm/updateGroup`) — reconstructing the same `GroupHandle = \"{ProviderHandle}/{GroupId}\"` that the live wire path produces, resolved through the provider identifier map (defaulting to \"git\").\n- **LoggingPlugin**: Cap `tauri::manager` and `tauri::manager::asset` to Warn, `tauri::webview` and `wry` to Info, to suppress the flood of expected 404 fallback probes for sourcemap/module URLs that WebKit auto-fetches with the wrong base under `tauri://localhost`.\n- **LocalPTYGetProfiles**: Rename `Arguments` → `args` (lowercase) to match VS Code's `ITerminalProfile.args` — the uppercase key silently mis-parsed and the profile picker fell back to `$SHELL`.\n- **SCM Effect**: Accept `git.openChange` / `git.openFile` as diff-forwarding aliases alongside `vscode.diff` / `$scm:openDiff`; these are the actual command IDs the built-in vscode.git extension uses on resource state entries.\n- **build.rs**: Normalize array formatting in `PropagatePostHogSentinel`.\n\nThe SCM panel now populates with groups and working-tree state at boot, and terminal profiles render with their configured arguments.",
			"SHA": "2db7957cc5af3113a94be7ee360e1f2cb34cb769"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T17:22:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1746,
				7
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Rename OTLP env vars and tighten default trace categories\n\nRename the baked compile-time environment variables `OTLPEndpoint` to `Pipe` and `OTLPEnabled` to `Emit` across build.rs, PostHogPlugin constants, runtime hydration, Cocoon process environment propagation, and OTLP span emitter docs. The shorter names reduce line noise in the env map and align with the single-word naming convention of sibling keys (`Capture`, `Beam`, `Brand`, `Report`).\n\nNarrow the `Trace` sentinel value in Info.plist from the catch-all `\"all\"` to an explicit comma-delimited list of active trace categories, ensuring debug log output only covers relevant subsystems instead of flooding stderr with every DevLog call.\n\nAlso fix a stale doc comment reference in CaptureAllowed.rs that mentioned `OTLPEnabled` instead of the current `Emit` toggle name.",
			"SHA": "b1ff14804289a99599bd3c0aab3c552e49564057"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T14:51:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1746,
				1
			],
			"Message": "Merge pull request #60 from CodeEditorLand/dependabot/github_actions/ad-m/github-push-action-1.3.0\n\nchore(deps): Bump ad-m/github-push-action from 1.1.0 to 1.3.0",
			"SHA": "2add8ef9dc6ce3535b0359c1e99417c0de6a04c6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T14:02:37Z",
